From ddbeca8e99ae1e5917afe4dde3085a48889da33f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:15:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(ui): a Home button and a start page with the recent
 projects

The top band has a Home button left of Donate. It shows a start page in
place of the dock: the recent projects (the #662 list, newest first, a
gone file greyed as missing), then Open project, New project and Back to
the project. A click on a project queues OpenRecent, so the unsaved
changes prompt is Open's. The page remembers the doc_version it opened
over and closes when the document changes. It shows at a start with no
file on the command line. The version label stays the rightmost toolbar
item.

The glyph is Tabler's home outline (MIT), with its SVG master and notice.
The site icon mirror takes home.png, the act-report.png that #1696 left
out, and the current LICENSES text.

Fixes #2384

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
